COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION
Article 19
(1) In providing protection to women and children victims of violence, the community may:
a. establish family partners at the kelurahan/village level coordinating with Desa Pakraman;
b. establish women and children protection units within community organizations;
c. conduct independent socialization of women's and children's rights;
d. provide first aid to victims; and
e. report to the competent authorities if violence against victims occurs in their environment.
(2) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out by individuals, Desa Pakraman, social community institutions, non-governmental organizations, educational institutions, religious institutions, private sector, and mass media.

CHAPTER VI
MINIMUM SERVICE STANDARDS
Article 10
(1) The MSS for Integrated Services for Women and Children Victims of Violence aims to guarantee that women and children victims of violence receive the minimum services needed.
(2) The MSS for Integrated Services for Women and Children Victims of Violence includes services for:
a. handling complaints/reports of victims of violence against women and children;
b. health services for women and children victims of violence;
c. social rehabilitation for women and children victims of violence;
d. law enforcement and legal assistance for women and children victims of violence;
e. repatriation and social reintegration for women and children victims of violence; and
f. in the event that victims experience trauma or illness that endangers themselves as a result of acts of violence requiring immediate assistance, the regional government is obligated to provide first aid no later than 7 (seven) days after the complaint is filed.

CHAPTER X
GUIDANCE AND SUPERVISION
Article 17
(1) The Regent provides guidance for the development of PPT. (2) Guidance as referred to in paragraph (1) includes: a. provision of implementation instructions;
b. guidance;
c. supervision;
d. monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of services for women and children victims of violence, as well as for the apparatus and the community.

REGENT OF TABANAN,
Considering : a. that acts of violence against women and children constitute violations of human rights and therefore their dignity and honor need to be protected and their right to life guaranteed in accordance with their nature without discrimination;
b. that to prevent and overcome violence against women and children, legal protection needs to be provided for women and children victims of violence;
c. that in the context of implementing protection for women and children victims of violence in Tabanan Regency, there is no regulatory basis yet;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation on the Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence;
In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 69 of 1958 concerning the Establishment of Level II Regions within the Level I Regions of Bali, West Nusa Tenggara and East Nusa Tenggara (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1958 Number 122, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1655);
