f. in the event that victims experience trauma or illness that endangers themselves as a result of acts of violence requiring immediate assistance, the regional government is obligated to provide first aid no later than 7 (seven) days after the complaint is filed.

REGENT OF TABANAN,
Considering : a. that acts of violence against women and children constitute violations of human rights and therefore their dignity and honor need to be protected and their right to life guaranteed in accordance with their nature without discrimination;
b. that to prevent and overcome violence against women and children, legal protection needs to be provided for women and children victims of violence;
c. that in the context of implementing protection for women and children victims of violence in Tabanan Regency, there is no regulatory basis yet;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation on the Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence;
In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 69 of 1958 concerning the Establishment of Level II Regions within the Level I Regions of Bali, West Nusa Tenggara and East Nusa Tenggara (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1958 Number 122, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1655);
3. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 165; Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);
4. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235), as has been amended several times most recently by Law Number 35 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 297, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5606);
5. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
6. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
7. Law Number 12 of 2011 concerning the Formation of Laws and Regulations (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2011 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5234);
8. Law Number 16 of 2011 concerning Legal Aid (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2011 Number 104, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5246);
9. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as has been amended several times most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);
10. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2008 concerning the Implementation of Women's Protection;
11. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 3 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for the Implementation of Child Protection;
12. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 1 of 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards in the Field of Integrated Services for Women and Children Victims of Violence;
13. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 5 of 2010 concerning Guidelines for the Establishment and Development of Integrated Service Centers;
14. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 02 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for Handling Child Victims of Violence;
15. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 19 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for the Empowerment of Women Victims of Violence;
16. Regional Regulation of Bali Province Number 6 of 2014 concerning Child Protection (Regional Gazette of Bali Province Year 2014 Number 6, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of Bali Province Number 6);
With the Mutual Approval of THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF TABANAN REGENCY and

Article 11
(1) SPM as referred to in Article 10 has performance indicators including:
a. coverage of women and children victims of violence who receive complaint handling by trained officers in integrated service units;
b. coverage of women and children victims of violence who receive health services by trained health workers at Puskesmas and Hospitals;
c. coverage of social rehabilitation services provided by trained social rehabilitation officers for women and children victims of violence in integrated service units;
d. coverage of spiritual guidance services provided by trained spiritual guidance officers for women and children victims of violence in integrated service units;
e. coverage of law enforcement from the investigation level to court decisions on cases of violence against women and children;
f. coverage of women and children victims of violence who receive legal aid services;
g. coverage of return services for women and children victims of violence; and
h. coverage of social reintegration services for women and children victims of violence.
(2) The determination of SPM performance indicators for the Integrated Service Field for Women and Children Victims of Violence as referred to in paragraph (1) constitutes minimum targets that must be achieved by integrated service units in stages.

CHAPTER XI
COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION
Article 19
(1) In providing protection to women and children victims of violence, the community may:
a. establish family partners at the kelurahan/village level coordinating with Desa Pakraman;
b. establish women and children protection units within community organizations;
c. conduct independent socialization of women's and children's rights;
d. provide first aid to victims; and
e. report to the competent authorities if violence against victims occurs in their environment.
(2) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out by individuals, Desa Pakraman, social community institutions, non-governmental organizations, educational institutions, religious institutions, private sector, and mass media.

CHAPTER X
GUIDANCE AND SUPERVISION
Article 17
(1) The Regent provides guidance for the development of PPT. (2) Guidance as referred to in paragraph (1) includes: a. provision of implementation instructions;
b. guidance;
c. supervision;
d. monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of services for women and children victims of violence, as well as for the apparatus and the community.

CHAPTER III
RIGHTS OF VICTIMS
Article 4
The rights of victims include:
a. protection from the family;
b. protection from the police;
c. protection from the prosecutor's office;
d. protection from the court;
e. protection from advocates;
f. protection from social institutions, or other parties either temporarily or based on the stipulation of a protection order from the court;
g. health services in accordance with medical needs;
h. special handling related to the confidentiality of victims;
i. assistance by social workers and legal aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
j. spiritual guidance services; and
k. victims have the right to determine their own decisions regarding which option will be implemented.

